id: mental-model:dave:christianity
title: "Dave / Christianity"
kind: mental-model
record_shape: header
status: draft
spec_version: mental-model.v0.1
template_ref: templates/mental-model.yawn
relationship_ref: relationship:dave:christianity
relationship_projection_ref: dave/christianity/relationship.yawn
relationship_revision: 2
relationship_disclosure_scope: public-safe
principal_ref: principal:dave
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Codex session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-30; built from Dave's stated request for a public-safe relationship conformance case. It records an inquiry purpose, not a religious identity or belief."
arena: "A private-to-public-safe inquiry into the relationship between Dave's current model and Christianity"
updated: 2026-09-30

relationship_view:
  canonical_relationship_ref: relationship:dave:christianity
  canonical_revision: 2
  public_projection_ref: dave/christianity/relationship.yawn
  disclosure_scope: public-safe
  rule: >
    This mental model is a permitted public View of the canonical relationship.
    It does not disclose private inference envelopes or their persisted output.

questions:
  - key: role
    answer: "A participant examining a relationship to a tradition, not a person whose identity or beliefs are inferred by this record."
  - key: relevance
    answer: "To inspect the model Dave is carrying around Christianity: what sources and people actually say, what is inferred, what remains unresolved, and what would change the model."
  - key: definition
    answer: "A public-safe, revisable model of Dave's inquiry relationship to Christianity, a diverse historical and living religious tradition."
  - key: inside
    answer: "A stated purpose, attributed sources and perspectives, boundaries, history, and a frontier question; none silently becomes Dave's belief, consent, or identity."
  - key: show
    answer: "Start with why this relationship is open, then inspect sources, perspectives, boundaries, history, and the next useful question."
  - key: assumptions
    answer: "That a tradition has many sources and interpretations, and that a source claim, an interpretation, and Dave's own position need separate attribution."
  - key: proof
    answer: "A reader can trace a displayed claim to an attributed source or proposal, see what remains unknown, and correct the model without rewriting its source."
  - key: lacuna
    answer: "Which parts of Christianity are relevant to Dave now, which sources he wants to examine, and which positions he endorses, if any."

concept:
  name: "Dave / Christianity"
  one_line: "A relationship record that helps Dave examine a tradition without mistaking the map, a source, or a route for a settled personal belief."
  inside:
    - name: "Purpose"
      glyph: "WHY"
      one_line: "Why this relationship is open before deciding which definition or source matters."
    - name: "Attribution"
      glyph: "↗"
      one_line: "A source, its reported speaker, an interpretation, and Dave's response remain separately named."
    - name: "Perspectives"
      glyph: "≠"
      one_line: "Different traditions, scholars, and readers may offer distinct or conditional answers without becoming a forced binary."
    - name: "Boundary"
      glyph: "⊘"
      one_line: "Historical voices are not live participants; no source claim becomes Dave's identity, consent, or authority."
    - name: "Frontier"
      glyph: "?"
      one_line: "The next question stays open until purpose, evidence, and the relationship make one useful."

show:
  - icon: WHY
    do: "Read the stated purpose before opening a definition or a debate."
    say: "Why is this relationship open for Dave now?"
  - icon: ↗
    do: "Open a claim with its source, attribution, interpretation, and uncertainty."
    say: "What does this source report, and what has been added in interpretation?"
  - icon: ≠
    do: "Compare relevant perspectives without treating popularity or agreement as truth."
    say: "Which distinctions in source, scope, definition, or evidence explain the difference?"
  - icon: ⊘
    do: "Inspect the participation and disclosure boundary before treating a voice as present."
    say: "Who is actually participating here, and who is only represented by a source?"
  - icon: "?"
    do: "Return to the current frontier instead of manufacturing a conclusion."
    say: "What question would most change orientation from this relationship?"

embody:
  - "Begin with the stated purpose; do not infer a religious identity, commitment, or belief from opening this model."
  - "Keep source, attributed speaker, interpretation, and Dave's recognition or endorsement separate."
  - "Represent historical figures, text authors, and interpreters as source-associated voices, never as live participants."
  - "Treat dave/christianity as a directional View into a relationship record, not as containment or proof of agreement."
  - "Offer a hold or a question when the source, scope, or authority is not clear."

assumptions:
  - text: "Christianity contains diverse historical sources, communities, and interpretations; this model does not select one as the whole tradition."
    epistemic_status: assumed
  - text: "A relationship record can preserve a source claim, interpretation, and personal response without collapsing them into one truth claim."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "Dave asked for a public-safe conformance case that does not infer or publish his religious identity or beliefs."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "A directional slash route is an address/View and does not establish containment, agreement, consent, or authority."
    epistemic_status: observed

proof:
  signals:
    - "A displayed claim identifies whether it is source-attributed, interpreted, proposed, or Dave-reported."
    - "A historical person or text can be represented without appearing as a live participant or decision holder."
    - "A correction preserves the earlier source and records what interpretation or view changed."
    - "A reader can distinguish the relationship's current purpose from any claim about Dave's beliefs."
  falsifier: "This model fails if it states or implies that Dave holds a religious identity or belief he has not explicitly supplied, treats a slash as containment, or presents a historical voice as a live participant."

lacunae:
  - "Which strand, community, historical period, or question within Christianity is relevant to Dave now."
  - "Which source materials Dave wants to inspect and which editions, translations, or interpretations matter for that inspection."
  - "What Dave recognizes, endorses, disputes, or prefers, if he chooses to record any of those positions."
  - "What relationship-specific Yawn, if any, would earn independent stewardship, continuity, or proof obligations."

sources:
  - text: "Dave's participant-provided relationship pressure test, 2026-09-30: requested a public-safe Dave / Christianity conformance case with purpose, attribution, boundaries, history, and frontier kept distinct."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "spec/ontology.md: relationship is a situated, changing coupling and is not automatically ownership, containment, agreement, or authority."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "core/RELATIONSHIP_FIRST_AGENT_ARENA.yawn: Relationship is structurally first; Observation is operationally first."
    epistemic_status: observed
  - text: "templates/mental-model.yawn: questions-first records keep why, perspective, inference status, and lacunae visible."
    epistemic_status: observed
